@startuml archetype-detection
title Use: route a new candidate to the right pipeline (v2)

skinparam shadowing false

start
:Candidate submits CV / portfolio / form;

:Collect signals;
note right
  * explicit self-declaration in the form
    ("I am a student / recent graduate",
     "I want to change field")
  * enrollment status / expected graduation
  * years of *relevant* professional experience
    (off-field part-time excluded)
  * education-block dominance vs work-block
  * recency: studies ongoing or just finished
  * domain of past work vs target role
end note

:Compute archetype scores (with confidence);

if (Explicit self-declaration?) then (yes)
  :Trust declaration as primary signal\n(but keep auto-signals to flag mismatch);
else (no / ambiguous)
  :Use weighted auto-signals;
endif

if (Substantial experience\nin a DIFFERENT target domain\n+ intent to switch?) then (yes)
  #FFE0B2:CAREER_SWITCHER;
  note right: diagram 12
elseif (Little/no relevant pro experience\nAND education is the dominant block?) then (yes)
  #C8E6C9:STUDENT_EARLY_CAREER;
  note right: diagrams 08-10
else (no)
  :BAU_EXPERIENCED;
  note right: diagram 06
endif

:Attach archetype + confidence to profile;
:Offer the user a one-click override\n(routing is a suggestion, not a verdict);

note right
  Detection is never silently final. The candidate confirms,
  the recruiter sees the archetype + confidence, and a
  borderline case can be scored under BOTH profiles.
end note
stop
@enduml
